    "details": "https://github.com/erlang/otp/security/advisories/GHSA-r5jr-mq46-vmhw\nreports:\n\n> A TLS/DTLS peer can crash the remote node by sending a certificate\n> chain containing two mutually cross-signed certificates in unordered\n> form. When the receiving side attempts to build a valid chain path, it\n> enters unbounded recursion between the two certificates (A issues B, B\n> issues A) with no cycle detection or depth limit. The call stack and\n> chain accumulator grow without bound until the process exhausts\n> available memory and the BEAM node crashes.\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0353",
